<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crown of Ireland Act 1542</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1541–1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Crown of Ireland Act was passed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-ireland">Irish Parliament</a> in June 1541, at the urging of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>, and created the title of King of Ireland for him and his successors. It replaced the Lordship of Ireland, held by English kings since the 12th century under a papal grant, with a Kingdom of Ireland, reflecting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s break with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The new title took effect in 1542.</p></div>
